{
  "name": "ok_request_attempt",
  "description": "The two event types that make a turn's provider traffic auditable at attempt level: request/header (one row per request built, naming why a fresh request exists and for which model) and assistant/attempt (one row per attempt that did NOT become the visible answer, with its retryable flag). Additive — no envelope change, no version bump (AGENTS.md rule 2). The successful attempt still lands as exactly one assistant/message, so a reader that folds only assistant/message sees the same answer it saw before these rows existed.",
